<title>UK: French govt may sell part of GAN insurer - paper.</title>
<headline>French govt may sell part of GAN insurer - paper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The French goverment is considering selling some of its shares in the state-owned insurer GAN to private investors in an effort to recapitalise the group and sell it off next year, the Financial Times said on Friday.</p>
<p>The report said the plans had the support of the European Commission which mentions the strategy in a draft judgement on GAN's recapitalisation. The FT said it obtained a copy of the document.</p>
<p>On October 23, GAN reported a consolidated net loss of 965 million French francs in the six months to June 30, compared with a loss of 387 million French francs in the same year-earlier period.</p>
<p>--London newsroom +44 171 5427717</p>
